# Optional ML and deep learning dependencies (umbrella)
# This is a convenience umbrella file that aggregates ML capability layers.
# For fine-grained control, install individual layers from ml-*.in files.
#
# No checked-in umbrella ML lock is generated from this file. Use explicit
# target-owned ML commands for supported lock artifacts.
#
# LAYERED ML DEPENDENCY STRATEGY
# ==============================
# This file documents the historical umbrella composition, but root
# `make install-ml` is fail-closed until a trusted umbrella lock contract
# exists again. Platform-specific and scripted-only layers are NOT included.
#
#   ml-core.in     Cross-platform ML baseline (torch, diffusers, transformers)
#   ml-raw.in      RAW camera file ingest (rawpy) - platform-scoped markers
#
# EXCLUDED from umbrella (opt-in only):
#   ml-sam2.in     SAM2 segmentation - SCRIPTED ONLY (non-standard install semantics)
#   ml-coreml.in   Apple CoreML acceleration - macOS only
#   ml-research.in Research/experimental extras - reserved for future use
#
# Install targets:
#   make install-ml-core    # supported Apple Silicon baseline
#   make install-ml-raw     # disabled: no trusted RAW lock contract
#   make install-ml         # disabled: no trusted umbrella lock contract
#
# For SAM2 or CoreML, use bootstrap script:
#   ./scripts/bootstrap/install_ml_stack.sh --profile core-cpu,sam2
#   ./scripts/bootstrap/install_ml_stack.sh --profile core-cpu,coreml
#
# Current supported Apple Silicon lock baseline for determinism:
#   torch==2.12.0, torchvision==0.27.0, open-clip-torch==3.3.0
# Cross-platform metadata in ml-core.in uses compatible lower bounds; only
# target-owned locks are install support promises.
#
# See requirements/README.md for full layering documentation.

# Include cross-platform ML capability layers only
-r ml-core.in
-r ml-raw.in
# NOTE: ml-sam2.in is EXCLUDED - requires scripted install (non-standard semantics)
# NOTE: ml-coreml.in is EXCLUDED - platform-specific (macOS only)
# NOTE: ml-research.in is EXCLUDED - opt-in only
